# ESP32 Traffic Light Controller

## Project Description

This project is a traffic light controller built using an ESP32 microcontroller and a 16x2 I2C LCD display. The system automatically controls Red, Yellow, and Green traffic signals according to predefined timing intervals. The LCD displays the current signal status along with a countdown timer, simulating the operation of a real-world traffic signal system.

---

## Components Used

- ESP32 Development Board
- 16x2 I2C LCD Display
- Red LED
- Yellow LED
- Green LED
- 3 × 220Ω Resistors
- Jumper Wires
- Wokwi Simulator
- PlatformIO (VS Code)

---

## Features

- Automatic traffic signal sequencing
- Red, Yellow, and Green signal control
- Real-time countdown timer on LCD display
- I2C communication between ESP32 and LCD
- State-machine based traffic light logic
- Simulated and tested using Wokwi
- Developed using PlatformIO and VS Code

